      "description": "Ten Thousand Buddha Hall (Tathagata Hall). Zhihua Si, Beijing\nThis impressive two-story hall holds the temple's main Buddha image.  The black roof tile on the temple's buildings indicates its non-imperial status; for all his power, Wang Zhen only rated as a commoner. Colored roof tiles were reserved for the nobility; green for princely buildings, or yellow for imperial ones.",
